  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Status at commit dde0d3f",
      "items": [
        "Phases 0–11 (minimal) complete: Phase 10 adds evaluation, the baseline and the Evaluation tab in the UI",
        "First live run: only demo_fr completed; the other 4 cases stopped when API credits ran out",
        "On demo_fr the baseline ties: traceability 85% vs 92%, coherence 4 vs 4, ~8x tokens",
        "PDF export of the blueprint not done: Markdown only"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Shared runner",
      "items": [
        "The CLI, the UI and the evaluation all create a Run; the evaluation uses automatic approval",
        "At the interrupt the runner exposes the strategy (pending); the answer resumes the graph with Command(resume)",
        "A failing node is recorded in the log; Retry restarts from the last checkpoint",
        "In the UI the Run lives in st.session_state; a stream interrupted by a click resumes from the checkpoint"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Evaluation (Phase 10)",
      "items": [
        "Same document to two systems: the multi-agent pipeline with auto-approve and a single prompt with no tools or validator",
        "Metrics: claim traceability, figures found in the document or the cited source, coherence 1–5 and trap (judge with a fixed rubric), tokens and seconds",
        "In the UI the evaluation starts by itself at the end of a run (toggle); the baseline comparison is a button",
        "rating.py prepares blind X/Y pairs for human rating"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Revision and validation",
      "items": [
        "revise only if the stage's latest validation has blocking issues and the counter is < MAX_REVISIONS (2)",
        "Rules first; the judge runs only if no rule blocks",
        "A rejection resets strategy_revisions; human_feedback stays in the state until approval"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Output",
      "items": [
        "The blueprint node writes blueprint.md; the runner writes log.txt line by line, then state.json and run.json",
        "run.json: status, error, decisions, tokens per model, seconds for the pipeline alone",
        "The blueprint is rendered from the state; only the executive summary is written by the LLM"
      ]
    }
  ]
}